  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Energy Districts Programme # Vietnam interventions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GEDP Vietnam is the foundational phase of a multi-year, multi-stage Vietnam ED/RE-ED programme, designed to progressively create a f unctioning national ED/RE-ED market by demonstrating viable pilots, strengthening institutional and regulatory capacities, and enabling systematic replication and scale-up across priority urban and industrial districts; it is a focused, catalytic and enabling initiative that complements existing sustainable cooling and urban climate programmes while establishing the national enabling conditions to mainstream ED/RE-ED (including district cooling) as a pillar of Vietnam#s energy transition and urban-industrial development agenda, and by supporting targeted policy and regulatory frameworks, strengthening institutional coordination across energy, urban planning and industrial sectors, and demonstrating viable ED/RE-ED business and investment models, it provides practical, scalable solutions to manage rising peak electricity demand, alleviate grid congestion, enhance climate resilience to extreme heat, and decarbonize urban and industrial energy use#bridging strategic planning and implementation and enabling a shift from isolated pilots toward a coherent, long-term approach integrated into urban master plans, industrial zones and energy sector reforms.</narrative>
  </description>
